d 'TWOPARTLOG': module to estimate two-part log regression model with an optimal zero-handling constant for independent variables containing zeros
d
d     twopartlog implements the two-part regression framework
d proposed by Donald Lien, Yue Hu, and Long Liu (2025) to handle   
d regression analysis where the independent variable contains
d zeros. It generalizes the Started Logarithm (GSLT) and Inverse   
d Hyperbolic Sine (GIHST) transformations by estimating the optimal
d constant c via concentrated non-linear least squares, treats	 
d zero values as a separate group via indicator variables, computes
d average elasticities, and conducts continuity tests at x =	0. 
d
d KW: log regression
d KW: two-part regression framework
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261018
d
d Author: Dereje Fedasa Hordofa,   Dire Dawa University, Ethiopia
d Support: email derejefedasaa@@gmail.com
d
f twopartlog.ado
f twopartlog.sthlp
